Error: Jet.NameAlreadyTaken: Pattern hole `{root}` would make a new `root`, but `root` already holds a value
  --> Tests/UI/pattern_hole_reuse_value.jet:1:70
    |
  1 | matches: fn(value: String, root: String) -> Bool { return value == "{root}jet" }
    |                                                                      ^^^^
 Why: A pattern hole introduces a new name; it does not compare with an existing value or refine it
 Fix: Wrap the pattern text in parentheses to compare with the existing value, or pick a new hole name to capture
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.NameAlreadyTaken
